        ],
        "text": "The case concerns whether Title III of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) applies to foreign\u2011flagged cruise ships that dock in United States ports."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioners, petitioners are American citizens who purchased cruise tickets in the United States and allege discrimination by Norwegian Cruise Line Ltd., a U.S.-based company, both on land and in U.S. waters."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Frederick",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0001-0011"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 32,
              "start": 32
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Frederick, respondent argues that the issue is one of congressional intent rather than congressional power."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Gregory G. Garre",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3a0fc2b63b9ac03869965db16cacd030a9987871042851b9b41a4a7edf44a61c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3a0fc2b63b9a-0002-0008"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 50,
              "start": 50
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Gregory G. Garre, amicus briefs argue that applying the ADA extraterritorially could create international conflict."
      }
    ],
